WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.730
The Amazon is the largest
tropical rainforest on Earth,

2
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.390
and most of it lies in Brazil.

3
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:11.750
Cattle ranching, then soy, and new
roads have cut deep into the forest.

4
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:16.070
Since 1988, Brazil's
space institute, INPE,

5
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.670
has measured how much forest
is cleared every year.

6
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:27.920
Now INPE's estimate for August 2025 to July
2026 is its lowest since records began.

7
00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.230
So what made the difference?

8
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:35.990
In this mission, you'll trace how losing
forest here affects places near and far.

9
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.350
Then you'll test each way of managing
the forest against the evidence.

10
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.510
Your mission: find out what made
the difference to Amazon clearing.
